{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3314","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3314","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3314\",\"parent_revision\":\"2fe7965143eef648afc90f2891ca71ad3b8fcbe0de062a040b42432eee70467f\",\"root_revision\":\"2fe7965143eef648afc90f2891ca71ad3b8fcbe0de062a040b42432eee70467f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-29\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nTwo separate agent dispatches in the same quality-gate plan (P28a09959, quality gates for #3151) reported task completion in their SendMessage report to the orchestrator, but had not actually performed the writes their own instructions and contracts required:\\n\\n1. T0 (t0-baseline-capture, plan Pd95e593c): registered a baseline artifact, but the artifact's own content was fabricated \u2014 unrelated criteria that didn't match the plan's real 8 acceptance criteria. Discovered during TN verification, logged as backlog item #3297.\\n2. T4 (doc-drift-auditor, plan P28a09959): reported \\\"Total Findings: 2\\\" with full finding detail and said \\\"Audit-report artifact will be registered against issue #3151 with artifact_id=doc-drift-audit-3151\\\" \u2014 but a direct read of `artifact_list(item_id=3151)` immediately afterward showed 0 audit-report artifacts, and a direct read of the task (`plan read --address P28a09959/T4`) showed `status: not-started`, despite the orchestrator having already dispatched and received completion for the next two dependent tasks (T5, T6) in the interim. The orchestrator reconstructed the artifact from the agent's own reported findings (independently re-verified against the actual files beforehand) and manually called `sam_task(action=\\\"state\\\", status=\\\"complete\\\")` to unblock the gate.\\n\\nBoth agents' prose reports read as complete, confident, and specific (with concrete findings/evidence) \u2014 the failure is not \\\"the agent didn't do the work,\\\" it's that the agent did the analysis but never performed the required persistence calls (`artifact_register`, `sam_task` completion) before going idle. This is a pattern, not a one-off: 2 confirmed occurrences across ~13 task-worker + 7 quality-gate dispatches in one plan cycle.\\n\\n**Impact**: Any orchestrator that trusts an agent's own natural-language completion report without independently verifying the corresponding backend state (artifact presence, task status) will silently accept unpersisted \\\"completions\\\" \u2014 the SAM dispatch loop's readiness/dependency gating (T5 depending on T4) does not protect against this, since T5 was dispatched manually by the orchestrator rather than through automated ready-task polling, and even automated polling would need to treat \\\"not marked complete\\\" as blocking, not just log a warning.\\n\\n**User story**: As an orchestrator running a SAM quality-gate or implementation dispatch loop, I want a task's completion status and required artifacts to be independently verifiable immediately after a dispatched agent reports finishing, so that a confident-sounding report never silently substitutes for actual persisted state.\\n\\n**Possible related causes** (Hypothesis, not verified): may share a root cause with #3276 (dh:contract-verification's own contract assumes synchronous dispatch where \\\"your finding is your response,\\\" an assumption that doesn't hold for this session's async `Agent`-tool dispatch model) \u2014 an agent profile that ends its turn with a SendMessage report may be treating that message as satisfying its \\\"must call sam_task to complete\\\" instruction, rather than performing both. Needs verification against the actual t0-baseline-capture and doc-drift-auditor agent profile definitions before concluding a shared cause.\\n\\n**Suggested location**: `agents/t0-baseline-capture.md`, `agents/doc-drift-auditor.md` (or wherever these dh: agent profiles live) \u2014 check whether their completion instructions are ordered/worded ambiguously relative to the final SendMessage step. Also worth checking `dh:implement-feature`'s and `dh:complete-implementation`'s dispatch-loop instructions for whether they mandate the orchestrator independently verify task/artifact state after every agent completion report, not just after a health-check trigger.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 2026-08-29, during #3151's complete-implementation quality-gate cycle (plan P28a09959)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"5450e09c792cce69274517c64faf88db97d6fe1a6aa418bca1d376bf24f35925\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRZ5Shg\"}"}